<h2>Where should the filter controls go on the account activity page?</h2>
<p class="subtitle">These are wireframes for placement only. The real controls will follow docs/ui-guidelines (tokens, labels above fields, sentence case). Click the one that feels right.</p>

<div class="options">
  <div class="option" data-choice="a" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">A</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Filter bar between the intro and the table</h3>
      <p>All controls are always visible. A labelled event type Select, a "Failed sign-ins only" checkbox, and a search field for device or location. A "Showing N of M events" line is announced to screen readers.</p>
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Account activity</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <p style="margin:0 0 10px">Every sign-in and account change from the last 90 days, newest first.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-end;padding:10px;border:1px solid #ccc;border-radius:6px">
            <label style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px;font-size:13px">Event type<select class="mock-input"><option>All events</option></select></label>
            <label style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px;font-size:13px">Search device or location<input class="mock-input" type="search"></label>
            <label style="font-size:13px"><input type="checkbox"> Failed sign-ins only</label>
            <button class="mock-button">Clear filters</button>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size:12px;margin:8px 0">Showing 8 of 48 events</p>
          <div class="placeholder">Table: When / Event / Device / Location / IP / Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="option" data-choice="b" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">B</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>One "Filter" button that opens a popover</h3>
      <p>The page stays quiet until someone asks for filters. The same controls sit inside a 360-wide popover. Active filters show as removable tags next to the button. It costs one extra click, and it needs focus management for the popover.</p>
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Account activity</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <p style="margin:0 0 10px">Every sign-in and account change from the last 90 days, newest first.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center">
            <button class="mock-button">Filter</button>
            <span style="font-size:12px;border:1px solid #888;border-radius:10px;padding:2px 8px">Sign-in failed &times;</span>
            <span style="font-size:12px;margin-left:auto">Showing 8 of 48 events</span>
          </div>
          <div style="width:220px;margin:6px 0 10px;padding:10px;border:1px solid #ccc;border-radius:6px;box-shadow:0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,.15);font-size:13px">
            Event type<br><select class="mock-input"><option>Sign-in failed</option></select><br>
            Search device or location<br><input class="mock-input" type="search">
          </div>
          <div class="placeholder">Table</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="option" data-choice="c" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">C</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Quick-filter groups plus search</h3>
      <p>A row of radio buttons styled as segments: All, Sign-ins, Failed sign-ins, Account changes. There is one search field beside it. Picking a group is the fastest option. It gives up picking any single one of the nine event types, unless the groups are an addition to A.</p>
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Account activity</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <p style="margin:0 0 10px">Every sign-in and account change from the last 90 days, newest first.</p>
          <fieldset style="display:flex;gap:0;flex-wrap:wrap;border:none;padding:0;margin:0 0 8px;align-items:center">
            <legend style="font-size:13px;margin-bottom:4px">Show</legend>
            <span style="border:1px solid #888;padding:4px 10px;font-size:13px;background:#ddd">All</span>
            <span style="border:1px solid #888;padding:4px 10px;font-size:13px">Sign-ins</span>
            <span style="border:1px solid #888;padding:4px 10px;font-size:13px">Failed sign-ins</span>
            <span style="border:1px solid #888;padding:4px 10px;font-size:13px">Account changes</span>
            <input class="mock-input" type="search" style="margin-left:12px" aria-label="Search">
          </fieldset>
          <p style="font-size:12px;margin:0 0 8px">Showing 48 of 48 events</p>
          <div class="placeholder">Table</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
